### =====================================================================
### POC Pontes — full demo scenario (IntelliJ HTTP client / VS Code REST Client)
### Prerequisite: application running (mvn spring-boot:run) with pontes.demo.enabled=true:
###   RTGS accounts EUROSYSTEM-DLT-TA (0), BANKAFRPP (10 M), BANKCDEFF (10 M), BANKBFRPP (5 M)
###   digital bond XS0000000001: 1,000 units held by BANKBFRPP (market DLT)
### =====================================================================
@host = http://localhost:8080

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. TARGET Services (RTGS / ESMIG): central bank money accounts
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### List of RTGS DCAs
GET {{host}}/api/target/accounts

### Technical account backing the cash tokens
GET {{host}}/api/target/accounts/EUROSYSTEM-DLT-TA

### Open an additional account (409 if already open)
POST {{host}}/api/target/accounts
Content-Type: application/json

{ "accountId": "DEUTDEFF", "owner": "Deutsche Bank", "initialBalance": 3000000 }

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. Market DLT (simulated Canton): securities positions
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### Position of BANKBFRPP (seller of the digital bond)
GET {{host}}/api/market-dlt/holdings/BANKBFRPP

### (optional) Primary issuance of another tokenised security
POST {{host}}/api/market-dlt/issuances
Content-Type: application/json

{ "party": "BANKBFRPP", "isin": "XS0000000002", "quantity": 500 }

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. Eurosystem DLT: cash token issuance (mint) by BANKCDEFF
###    RTGS BANKCDEFF → EUROSYSTEM-DLT-TA via the Trigger Backend, then tokens issued (asynchronous)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### Mint request: EUR 2,000,000 of cash tokens
# @name mint
POST {{host}}/api/dlt/mint
Content-Type: application/json

{ "participant": "BANKCDEFF", "amount": 2000000 }

### Operation tracking (PENDING_RTGS → COMPLETED)
GET {{host}}/api/dlt/operations/mint-0cd41f71-9a74-451d-bb0a-da81584740ad

### BANKCDEFF wallet on the DLT
GET {{host}}/api/dlt/wallets/BANKCDEFF

### RTGS: BANKCDEFF debited, technical account credited
GET {{host}}/api/target/accounts

### Mint rejected: insufficient RTGS funds (operation REJECTED)
POST {{host}}/api/dlt/mint
Content-Type: application/json

{ "participant": "BANKBFRPP", "amount": 999000000 }

###
GET {{host}}/api/dlt/operations/mint-12ecdd20-5afb-40d9-b732-01feb6bd3338

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4. DvP option A (CASH_TOKEN) — Hash Link protocol (Pontes URD v1.0, §4.2)
###    BANKBFRPP delivers 100 XS0000000001 to BANKCDEFF against EUR 1,000,000 of cash tokens
###    Pontes only knows the cash leg; the ISIN and quantity are only sent to the market DLT.
###    The seller / payer / requester fields stand in for the identity authenticated by ESMIG.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### 4.1 Phase 1 — the seller initialises the DvP: Pontes generates the keys and returns only their hashes (201)
###     timeoutSeconds optional: default 600 s (pontes.hash-link.default-timeout), maximum 3,600 s
POST {{host}}/api/eii/dvp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tradeReference": "TRADE-A-0001",
  "seller": "BANKBFRPP",
  "buyer": "BANKCDEFF",
  "cashAmount": 1000000,
  "cashLeg": "CASH_TOKEN"
}

### 4.2 Replay the same tradeReference: idempotent (same dvpId, same hashes, no new instance)
POST {{host}}/api/eii/dvp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tradeReference": "TRADE-A-0001",
  "seller": "BANKBFRPP",
  "buyer": "BANKCDEFF",
  "cashAmount": 1000000,
  "cashLeg": "CASH_TOKEN"
}

### 4.3 Phase 1 — the seller locks its securities on the market DLT in a Hash-Link Contract (201)
###     409 if the available position is insufficient
POST {{host}}/api/market-dlt/hash-link-contracts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "dvpId": "dvp-28fc06b9-a4a1-4d8e-825b-d2a74b15457e",
  "seller": "BANKBFRPP",
  "buyer": "BANKCDEFF",
  "isin": "XS0000000001",
  "quantity": 100,
  "executionKeyHash": "ac28e12f32bfbc53bb54867cd32922d106051ea33dd60872b8395b780f476290",
  "cancellationKeyHash": "feb60dee43360b7b7ec688d079c3024ba6dd72a10a492fd435f804476e97bbef",
  "timeout": "2026-09-28T13:56:08.716430Z"
}

### 4.4 Phase 1 — the buyer checks the parameters (Initialisation Query): status INITIALISED
GET {{host}}/api/eii/dvp/dvp-28fc06b9-a4a1-4d8e-825b-d2a74b15457e

### ... and the Hash-Link Contract on the market DLT: same hashes, status LOCKED
GET {{host}}/api/market-dlt/hash-link-contracts/dvp-28fc06b9-a4a1-4d8e-825b-d2a74b15457e

### 4.5 The Execution Key is not revealed before payment: 409
POST {{host}}/api/eii/dvp/dvp-28fc06b9-a4a1-4d8e-825b-d2a74b15457e/reveal-key
Content-Type: application/json

{ "requester": "BANKCDEFF" }

### 4.6 Phase 2a — the buyer pays: 200, paymentStatus SETTLED, Execution Key in the response
###     Payment reference <dvpId>-P1 (one per attempt, idempotent on the DLT side)
POST {{host}}/api/eii/dvp/dvp-28fc06b9-a4a1-4d8e-825b-d2a74b15457e/payment
Content-Type: application/json

{ "payer": "BANKCDEFF" }

### 4.7 Reveal Key: the buyer can also obtain the Execution Key afterwards (keyType EXECUTION)
POST {{host}}/api/eii/dvp/dvp-28fc06b9-a4a1-4d8e-825b-d2a74b15457e/reveal-key
Content-Type: application/json

{ "requester": "BANKCDEFF" }

### 4.8 A third party cannot obtain any key: 403
POST {{host}}/api/eii/dvp/dvp-28fc06b9-a4a1-4d8e-825b-d2a74b15457e/reveal-key
Content-Type: application/json

{ "requester": "BANKAFRPP" }

### 4.9 Invalid key presented to the Hash-Link Contract: 400, securities still locked
POST {{host}}/api/market-dlt/hash-link-contracts/dvp-28fc06b9-a4a1-4d8e-825b-d2a74b15457e/execute
Content-Type: application/json

{ "key": "feb60dee43360b7b7ec688d079c3024ba6dd72a10a492fd435f804476e97bbef" }

### 4.10 Phase 2a — the buyer presents the Execution Key: securities delivered (EXECUTED)
POST {{host}}/api/market-dlt/hash-link-contracts/dvp-28fc06b9-a4a1-4d8e-825b-d2a74b15457e/execute
Content-Type: application/json

{ "key": "15d5794dc29c4bb3527aa5b1230e7e229282b46ed2f718e5e63405ef062a94a7" }

### Securities positions: BANKBFRPP 900, BANKCDEFF 100
GET {{host}}/api/market-dlt/holdings/BANKCDEFF

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4a. DvP option A failing: payment refused, then expiry
###    BANKBFRPP sells 10 XS0000000001 to BANKAFRPP, which has no cash tokens. Short timeout (30 s).
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### Initialisation with timeoutSeconds = 30
POST {{host}}/api/eii/dvp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tradeReference": "TRADE-A-0002",
  "seller": "BANKBFRPP",
  "buyer": "BANKAFRPP",
  "cashAmount": 100000,
  "cashLeg": "CASH_TOKEN",
  "timeoutSeconds": 30
}

> {%
    client.global.set("dvpAko", response.body.dvpId);
    client.global.set("dvpAkoExecHash", response.body.executionKeyHash);
    client.global.set("dvpAkoCancelHash", response.body.cancellationKeyHash);
    client.global.set("dvpAkoTimeout", response.body.timeout);
%}

### The seller locks the securities
POST {{host}}/api/market-dlt/hash-link-contracts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "dvpId": "{{dvpAko}}",
  "seller": "BANKBFRPP",
  "buyer": "BANKAFRPP",
  "isin": "XS0000000001",
  "quantity": 10,
  "executionKeyHash": "{{dvpAkoExecHash}}",
  "cancellationKeyHash": "{{dvpAkoCancelHash}}",
  "timeout": "{{dvpAkoTimeout}}"
}

### Payment refused: 422, paymentStatus REJECTED (insufficient tokens), no key revealed.
### The instance stays INITIALISED: the buyer can retry (reference <dvpId>-P2) until the timeout.
POST {{host}}/api/eii/dvp/{{dvpAko}}/payment
Content-Type: application/json

{ "payer": "BANKAFRPP" }

### The seller requests the Cancellation Key before the timeout: 409
POST {{host}}/api/eii/dvp/{{dvpAko}}/reveal-key
Content-Type: application/json

{ "requester": "BANKBFRPP" }

### Wait 30 s, then: the seller obtains the Cancellation Key (keyType CANCELLATION), DvP EXPIRED
POST {{host}}/api/eii/dvp/{{dvpAko}}/reveal-key
Content-Type: application/json

{ "requester": "BANKBFRPP" }

> {% client.global.set("dvpAkoCancelKey", response.body.key); %}

### Payment after the timeout: 422 REJECTED
POST {{host}}/api/eii/dvp/{{dvpAko}}/payment
Content-Type: application/json

{ "payer": "BANKAFRPP" }

### The seller presents the Cancellation Key to the Hash-Link Contract: securities returned (CANCELLED)
POST {{host}}/api/market-dlt/hash-link-contracts/{{dvpAko}}/cancel
Content-Type: application/json

{ "key": "{{dvpAkoCancelKey}}" }

### BANKBFRPP position: the 10 units are available again
GET {{host}}/api/market-dlt/holdings/BANKBFRPP

### Wallets after DvP A
GET {{host}}/api/dlt/wallets

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### 5. DvP option B (T2) — cash leg settled directly in the RTGS, asynchronous finality
###    BANKBFRPP delivers 200 XS0000000001 to BANKAFRPP against EUR 2,000,000 in CeBM
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### 5.1 Phase 1 — initialisation by the seller (201)
POST {{host}}/api/eii/dvp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tradeReference": "TRADE-B-0001",
  "seller": "BANKBFRPP",
  "buyer": "BANKAFRPP",
  "cashAmount": 2000000,
  "cashLeg": "T2"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("dvpB", response.body.dvpId);
    client.global.set("dvpBExecHash", response.body.executionKeyHash);
    client.global.set("dvpBCancelHash", response.body.cancellationKeyHash);
    client.global.set("dvpBTimeout", response.body.timeout);
%}

### 5.2 Phase 1 — securities locked in the Hash-Link Contract
POST {{host}}/api/market-dlt/hash-link-contracts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "dvpId": "{{dvpB}}",
  "seller": "BANKBFRPP",
  "buyer": "BANKAFRPP",
  "isin": "XS0000000001",
  "quantity": 200,
  "executionKeyHash": "{{dvpBExecHash}}",
  "cancellationKeyHash": "{{dvpBCancelHash}}",
  "timeout": "{{dvpBTimeout}}"
}

### 5.3 Initialisation Query by the buyer
GET {{host}}/api/eii/dvp/{{dvpB}}

### 5.4 Phase 2a — payment: 202, paymentStatus PENDING (DVP_CASH_LEG trigger sent to T2)
POST {{host}}/api/eii/dvp/{{dvpB}}/payment
Content-Type: application/json

{ "payer": "BANKAFRPP" }

### 5.5 Tracking: PAYMENT_PENDING → SETTLED on T2 finality
###     (if T2 rejects the payment, the instance goes back to INITIALISED with lastRejectionReason)
GET {{host}}/api/eii/dvp/{{dvpB}}

### 5.6 Reveal Key by the buyer once SETTLED (409 while PAYMENT_PENDING)
POST {{host}}/api/eii/dvp/{{dvpB}}/reveal-key
Content-Type: application/json

{ "requester": "BANKAFRPP" }

> {% client.global.set("dvpBExecKey", response.body.key); %}

### 5.7 The buyer presents the Execution Key: securities delivered
POST {{host}}/api/market-dlt/hash-link-contracts/{{dvpB}}/execute
Content-Type: application/json

{ "key": "{{dvpBExecKey}}" }

### Lock refused: insufficient securities position at the seller (409)
POST {{host}}/api/market-dlt/hash-link-contracts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "dvpId": "dvp-unknown",
  "seller": "BANKBFRPP",
  "buyer": "BANKAFRPP",
  "isin": "XS0000000001",
  "quantity": 1000000,
  "executionKeyHash": "{{dvpBExecHash}}",
  "cancellationKeyHash": "{{dvpBCancelHash}}",
  "timeout": "{{dvpBTimeout}}"
}

### Invalid initialisation: 400 (Problem Details)
POST {{host}}/api/eii/dvp
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tradeReference": "", "seller": "BANKBFRPP", "buyer": "BANKAFRPP", "cashAmount": 0, "cashLeg": "T2" }

### Timeout out of bounds (> 3,600 s): 400
POST {{host}}/api/eii/dvp
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tradeReference": "TRADE-B-9999", "seller": "BANKBFRPP", "buyer": "BANKAFRPP", "cashAmount": 1000, "cashLeg": "T2", "timeoutSeconds": 7200 }

### All DvP instances (Pontes view: cash leg only)
GET {{host}}/api/eii/dvp

### Final securities positions
GET {{host}}/api/market-dlt/holdings/BANKAFRPP

###
GET {{host}}/api/market-dlt/holdings/BANKCDEFF

###
GET {{host}}/api/market-dlt/holdings/BANKBFRPP

### Triggers processed by the Trigger Backend (TOKEN_MINT, DVP_CASH_LEG, ...)
GET {{host}}/api/t2/triggers

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### 6. Redemption (redeem): BANKCDEFF destroys EUR 500,000 of tokens and gets the CeBM back
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{host}}/api/dlt/redeem
Content-Type: application/json

{ "participant": "BANKCDEFF", "amount": 500000 }

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### 7. DLT integrity
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### Transaction ledger (MINT / TRANSFER / BURN)
GET {{host}}/api/dlt/ledger

### Verification: valid chain and tokensInCirculation = balance of the EUROSYSTEM-DLT-TA account
GET {{host}}/api/dlt/ledger/verify

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### 8. Monitoring
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### Structure of the bounded contexts (Spring Modulith)
GET {{host}}/actuator/modulith

###
GET {{host}}/actuator/health
